    "result_text": "Build succeeds, all tests green. The audit line confirms the new behavior: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E` (region `NSW` from postcode `2000`, then 8 upper-case hex of SHA-256).\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, with all derived values following from it.\n\n**New identity** \u2014 `CustomerCodeAssigner`\n- Now builds `owner.getRegion() + \"-\" + HASH8`, where `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (the telephone is already E.164-normalized by the validator before this runs).\n- Dropped the per-city sequence entirely, so it no longer depends on `ClinicService` (`countOwnersByCity` stays \u2014 still used by `CityCapacityChecker`).\n\n**Region + locality** \u2014 `Owner`\n- Added `getRegion()` (the postcode \u2192 city \u2192 `UNKNOWN` derivation that previously lived in `getLocality`), used as the `REGION` segment of the customer code \u2014 single source of truth.\n- `getLocality()` now reads the identity: the segment before the first `-` of the customer code, falling back to `getRegion()` until a code is assigned. Locality is thus tied to the region-and-hash identity.\n\n**Automatically follow the new code** (no logic change needed, they already read `customerCode`):\n- `getMembershipNumber()` \u2192 `<customerCode>-M<YY>`\n- `getCheckDigit()` \u2192 Luhn over the code's digits\n- `OwnerCreationAuditLogger` \u2192 logs the new `customerCode`\n\n**Reuse, not duplication**\n- Extracted the SHA-256 \u2192 leading-upper-hex logic into `model/Sha256Hex.prefix(value, length)`, and refactored `HouseholdMatcher.householdId` (12 chars) to use it alongside the new customer code (8 chars), removing its inline digest code.\n\nAlso updated the stale javadoc example and the OpenAPI descriptions for `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` to match the new identity.",
